hits.text:
Claude Opus 5.5 in the desktop app can read and write your whole Obsidian vault, and the setup is 3 steps and one config file

it searches your notes, opens files, creates new ones and writes under the exact heading you name

your second brain finally gets a layer that thinks on top of it

the 3 steps:

1. in Obsidian, install the "Local REST API" plugin, switch it on and copy the API key

2. open the Claude Desktop config:

- Mac: ~/Library/Application Support/Claude/claude_desktop_config.json
- Windows: %APPDATA%/Claude/claude_desktop_config.json

3. add this block:

{
  "mcpServers": {
    "mcp-obsidian": {
      "command": "uvx",
      "args": ["mcp-obsidian"],
      "env": {
        "OBSIDIAN_API_KEY": "your_key_here",
        "OBSIDIAN_HOST": "127.0.0.1",
        "OBSIDIAN_PORT": "27124"
      }
    }
  }
}

> restart Claude and you're set

then type "find every note about pricing and save one summary" and watch it happen 👇

